      "outcome": "A fresh reviewer will establish whether the compact delivery loop is understandable and genuinely playable without relying on the implementation author's expectations. The result will identify any experience defect that should block the founder review, while preserving what was actually observed rather than converting taste into a test claim.\n\nExact contract. In repo slug swift-arrival, play only exact candidate commit a1d96fe4ce7280501f3d193fc3c3058a23e8a914, descended from baseline 84ff1745b29267708599e94036ec6f7a2a7e0457. This is independent evidence Work: do not change source, tests, assets, candidate commits, or the producer's existing evidence. Before inspecting the producer's playtest bundle or implementation details, launch a fresh native host and client using the candidate's own documented surfaces and attempt the bounded route as a new player. Probe the real installed capabilities first; do not substitute headless assertions for native play. Exercise and observe: initial control and objective comprehension; view-relative forward/strafe movement after meaningful mouse-look changes; blocked movement against visibly solid truck/world boundaries; pickup, deliberate drop away from the destination, recovery and re-pickup; entering and leaving the driver seat; bounded W/S driving; unloading both outside and inside the valid destination; host-authoritative player, vehicle, cargo and completion state visible to the client; and recovery from ordinary mistakes without restart or soft lock. Attempt at least one adverse interaction order a reasonable new player might try. Record where the view, geometry, feedback, or control mapping misleads you, including whether any debug presentation materially obstructs play. Distinguish direct observation, deterministic probe output, and product judgement. Do not call mechanics fun or founder-ready merely because probes pass.\n\nPreserve a compact native evidence bundle outside the repo with the exact candidate