      "outcome": "The compact delivery will require the intended pickup, drive, seat-exit, and unload journey instead of allowing the crate to be carried directly to the nearby bay. This preserves the truck as the core of the experience and makes completion truthful.\n\nExact contract. Repo slug swift-arrival, start from exact base commit 09fe09d30c65b811c0904508525a6ab8af02145c. Treat /company/inputs/exp11-referee-r9 as the superseding blind native observation: its action trace and final pixels show ON FOOT, DELIVERY COMPLETE, and ROUTE 0 / 40 m after walking the crate from the truck to the yellow bay without entering or driving the truck. Diagnose the smallest host-authoritative cause and repair the delivery state machine so unloading/completion is rejected until the authoritative journey has actually advanced through truck driving to the route destination and a valid post-arrival seat exit. Client HUD feedback must explain the unmet stage without falsely declaring destination reached or delivery complete. Preserve view-relative movement and driving, physical collision boundaries, mouse look, pickup/drop/recovery, host-authoritative shared player/vehicle/cargo/delivery state, placeholder assets, and the bounded local route. Do not solve this with presentation-only gating, a client-only check, hidden teleport, clamp-only collision, broad content, third-party assets, publishing, deployment, or external effects. Extend deterministic probes with a negative on-foot carry bypass from route 0 that must remain incomplete, plus positive pickup-drive-arrive-exit-unload completion and ordinary recovery. Run a fresh native X11 host/client journey showing the repaired positive route and the rejected starting-bay bypass. Commit all source and test changes in the Attempt workspace. Report exact observations, known limits, and anything not verified; deterministic probes establish mechanics, not feel.",
